228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (What is a Data Void? A data void is a search engine "information gap" where high-quality or reliable content for a specific query is non-existent, often because the topic is brand-new, niche, or uses a strategically invented term.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (How it influences RAG: When a RAG system encounters a data void, it is forced to retrieve low-authority or "poisoned" content from the only available sources \(often propaganda\), which the LLM then synthesizes into a confident and authoritative-sounding response.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
